--- INVARIANT ASSERTIONS DELIBERATELY EXEMPTED BY A VECTOR (the vector says why, here) ---
    An exemption is a check the VECTOR switched off, not one the harness could not run. It is
    admissible only for a shape where the REFERENCE ORACLE ITSELF violates the invariant and the
    implementation reproduces it, because there the assertion would be a claim about the oracle
    rather than about the port — and that is a graded-domain question, not a harness one. Every
    exemption below is named, scoped to one vector, and carries its own reason in full.
    THAT SENTENCE HAS TWO CONJUNCTS AND BOTH ARE NOW ASSERTED, in different places and with
    different consequences. (1) THE ORACLE CONJUNCT is decided OFFLINE, from the vector file
    alone, in the EXEMPTION GROUNDING section below: the exempted invariant is re-run against the
    schedule the CAPTURE recorded and must come back VIOLATED there, or the vector is refused.
    (2) THE PORT CONJUNCT is a statement about THIS RUN and is measured in the PORT CONJUNCT
    section below: the exempted invariant is run again, against the schedule THE IMPLEMENTATION
    RETURNED, and what it said is printed beside every exemption here. It is REPORTED, never
    refused — a port that satisfies an invariant the oracle violates has DIVERGED, and a
    divergence is the cell diff's finding, not a second admissibility verdict that could disagree
    with it. Until this run it was asserted by nothing, and the sentence above claimed it anyway.
    T116-G8-FAMB-N104 — principal_portions_sum_to_disbursed [EXEMPT]
        REASON: GATE G-8, FAMILY B, EXEMPTED BECAUSE THE REFERENCE ORACLE GENUINELY DOES NOT AMORTIZE THIS SHAPE -- not because the port is being excused. The oracle advances 1 minor unit and its own principal column repays 0: every repayment row carries principal 0.00 and its totalPrincipalAmount reads 0.00. The Go port reproduces that CELL FOR CELL (0 divergent cells over this vector's graded money cells, measured; see graded_against evidence), so there is no port-vs-oracle divergence for this invariant to arbitrate: asserting it here would be asserting that the ORACLE is wrong, which is a graded-domain amendment and a hard `user` gate (G-8 options (b) and (c)), not a check the harness may make on its own authority. THE EXEMPTION IS SCOPED TO THIS ONE CAPTURED SHAPE. It is NOT a statement that 600.0 % p.a. is exempt: the sibling vector T116-G8-CLEAN-N103, one repayment shorter at the same rate and the same principal, amortizes normally and carries NO exemption at all.
        PORT CONJUNCT: REPRODUCED — the schedule the implementation RETURNED violates
            this invariant too, which is the second half of the sentence above: principal advanced 1 minor units, principal repaid 0 minor units, difference -1
    T116-G8-FAMB-N104 — principal_amortizes_to_zero [EXEMPT]
        REASON: GATE G-8, FAMILY B, same shape and same reason. The final row's outstanding balance is 1 minor unit because the loan was never repaid, not because a balance memo went stale: the balance column is 0.01 on EVERY row, the principal column is 0.00 on every row, and the port returns exactly that. Family A -- where the principal column DOES sum to the disbursement and only the final balance is stale -- is a different phenomenon, is a CELL DIFF rather than an invariant failure, and is NOT covered by this exemption; an exemption cannot cure a parity diff and T116 does not attempt one.
        PORT CONJUNCT: REPRODUCED — the schedule the implementation RETURNED violates
            this invariant too, which is the second half of the sentence above: final row (REPAYMENT, due 2032-09-01) leaves 1 minor units outstanding, not 0
