--- EXEMPTION GROUNDING (every exemption re-run against the schedule ITS OWN VECTOR recorded) ---
    An exemption is admissible only where the REFERENCE ORACLE ITSELF violates the invariant. That
    is asserted, not assumed: each exempted invariant is re-run against the vector's own recorded
    schedule, honouring that vector's unrecorded_fields, and must come back VIOLATED there. This
    section reports the ORACLE conjunct only; whether the PORT reproduces the oracle's behaviour is
    a grading-time question and nothing here asserts it. Three verdicts are INADMISSIBLE, refused
    in Admit and never a warning: DECORATION (the invariant holds OUTRIGHT on the oracle's own
    numbers, with no assertion withheld, so the exemption silences nothing and only inflates the
    count above), NOT-EVALUABLE (the invariant has nothing to assert here at all, with nothing
    withdrawn) and SCHEDULE-UNREADABLE (the recorded rows do not parse into a schedule). A fourth,
    UNDETERMINED-ON-THE-RECORD, is REPORTED AND ADMITTED: this vector's own unrecorded_fields
    withdrew a cell the invariant reads, so the record is SILENT — which is not evidence against
    the exemption, and refusing it would kill a legitimate vector for a gap in the CAPTURE
    (finding T225-F1). It is counted apart from GROUNDED because it is not evidence either way.
    INSPECTED 51 loaded vector(s); 2 of them exempt at least one invariant; 4 exemption declaration(s) examined.
    4 GROUNDED (the recorded schedule VIOLATES the exempted invariant), 0 UNGROUNDED.
    0 UNDETERMINED-ON-THE-RECORD (a cell the invariant reads was never recorded; admitted, not evidence).

--- EXEMPTION CITATIONS (which observation each admissible exemption rests on) ---
    An exemption's whole argument is that THE REFERENCE ORACLE WAS OBSERVED TO BEHAVE THIS WAY.
    Its `reason` is free prose and always was; until finding T222-F4 was closed, nothing required
    that prose to point at anything, so an OBSERVATION and an ASSERTION were indistinguishable to
    this harness. The citation is MINTED by the harness, not read from the vector, and it is
    refused in Admit unless all three components resolve: the committed capture ARTEFACT exists
    in this repository and is non-empty; the capture CASE ID occurs inside that artefact's bytes
    (a bundle citation that names no case in the bundle is a page that is not in the book); and
    the RECORD'S OWN SENTENCE — the exempted invariant re-run against the captured schedule — is
    non-empty. The byte offsets below are the proof the artefact was opened.
