--- PORT CONJUNCT (every exempted invariant re-run against the schedule THE IMPLEMENTATION RETURNED) ---
    The exemption sentence has two conjuncts: the oracle violates the invariant, AND the
    implementation reproduces it. The section above asserts the first, offline, and refuses when
    it fails. This asserts the second, on THIS run's output, and REPORTS rather than refuses: a
    port that SATISFIES an invariant the oracle violates has diverged from the oracle, which is a
    parity finding the cell diff owns. Nothing in this section can fail a vector, and nothing in
    it is a licence: DIVERGED here means the exemption is excusing a behaviour the port does not
    actually have, which is worth a reader's attention even when every graded cell matched.
    INSPECTED 4 exempted assertion(s) on the graded vectors.
    4 REPRODUCED (the returned schedule violates the exempted invariant too), 0 DIVERGED, 0 COULD NOT SAY.

--- INVARIANT ASSERTIONS THAT COULD NOT RUN (a cell the capture never recorded) ---
    An invariant reads the schedule the implementation RETURNED. Where the implementation could not
    compute a cell — only the self-test replay ever can't, and only for a cell the vector's own
    unrecorded_fields withdrew — the assertions that read it are DECLARED not-applicable here rather
    than run against the stand-in. Both directions of that defect were live before this section
    existed: balance_roll_forward went RED on a placeholder, and principal_amortizes_to_zero went
    quietly GREEN on one, which is the worse half. A check that stops checking says so, in writing.
    NONE — every invariant assertion ran, on cells somebody actually observed.

